  "title": "Three conjugations: -ar, -er, -ir (present, Spanish verbs in English)",
  "lesson": {
    "kind": "review",
    "focusPoint": null,
    "points": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "heading": "Overview",
        "body": "This week you learned to conjugate three Spanish verb families in the present: -ar, -er, and -ir. A 10-year-old can do this alone by always naming stem and ending.\n\nLet's keep going together. tools to say out loud: conjugate = change the verb for the person; stem = what remains after dropping -ar/-er/-ir; ending = the new tip (-o, -as, -a or -es, -e).\n\nPráctica: Ahora te toca a ti. Say one verb from each family in I/you/he and name its stem before the ending.\n\nError común: Antes de terminar, un aviso. : Before we finish, one warning. Using -as for every family, even -er and -ir."
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "heading": "Point 1",
        "body": "Today we walk through this idea step by step. First conjugation ends in -ar. Model cantar: canto, cantas, canta. Stem = cant-. Endings = -o, -as, -a. The same pattern works for hablar and estudiar.\n\nLet's keep going together. step: cantar → drop -ar → cant- → add ending for the person.\n\nPráctica: Ahora te toca a ti. Write yo/tú/él for cantar and estudiar. Underline the stem and circle the ending in each form.\n\nError a corregir: Vigila este tropiezo frecuente: : Before we finish, one warning. Writing yo cantar instead of yo canto."
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "heading": "Point 2",
        "body": "Today we walk through this idea step by step. Second conjugation ends in -er. Model comer: como, comes, come. Stem = com-. Endings for I/you/he = -o, -es, -e (not the -ar set).\n\nLet's keep going together. compare: tú cantas (-ar uses -as) mientras que tú comes (-er uses -es). Same person, different family.\n\nPráctica: Ahora te toca a ti. Conjugate comer and beber for I/you/he. Mark stem and ending. Write one sentence with comes.\n\nError común: No te quedes con esta confusión: : Before we finish, one warning. tú comas. Correct: tú comes."
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "heading": "Point 3",
        "body": "Today we walk through this idea step by step. Third conjugation ends in -ir. Model vivir: vivo, vives, vive. Stem = viv-. Endings for I/you/he = -o, -es, -e. Nosotros uses -imos (vivimos), not -emos.\n\nLet's keep going together. step: vivir → viv- → vivo / vives / vive.\n\nPráctica: Ahora te toca a ti. Conjugate vivir and escribir for I/you/he. Mark stem and ending. Write one sentence with vive.\n\nError a corregir: Corrige a tiempo esta idea: : Before we finish, one warning. yo vive. Correct: yo vivo."
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "heading": "Synthesis",
        "body": "Today we walk through this idea step by step. Synthesis: if you can point to the stem and the ending, you understand the engine of conjugation for all three families.\n\nLet's keep going together. keep the three stems clear: cant- / com- / viv-. Then choose the ending for the person.\n\nPráctica: Ahora te toca a ti. Explain conjugate, stem, and ending to someone at home with one example from each family (-ar, -er, -ir).\n\nError común: Diferéncialo con claridad: : Before we finish, one warning. Memorizing full words without seeing stem + ending as two pieces."
      }
    ],
    "summary": ""
  },
